# Build-context excludes for the prod-profile app image builds (M1-379).
#
# The two app Dockerfiles set their build context to the repo root (the full
# multi-module reactor builds inside the image), so the context is the whole
# checkout. Keep stale host build output and the large git/agent state dirs out
# of every `docker compose --profile prod build` — they are regenerated by the
# in-image `mvn clean install` and would only bloat the context transfer.
target/
**/target/
.git/
.claude/
# Runtime state, never a build input (M1-564): operator secrets
# (secrets.env, signal-private.env) and messenger identity stores must
# not enter the build context, and the signal-cli daemon's root-owned
# data dir breaks the classic builder's context walk outright
# ("checking context: can't stat") on any host with a provisioned
# Signal adapter.
prod/runtime/
